# Section D calibration, candidate M. Independent reading before the stored fields.
FG-M-22cae42396 || cls=MX mod=DEFAULT dom=PE rel=PE pol=TST-011~ conf=M || actor=test author; act=coverage is diagnostic, not a target; prioritize meaningful behavior, edge cases, risky integrations; trig=test planning; scope=testing skill; exc=none; time=test design; enf=text || test=First sentence fits TST-011 on coverage percentage. Prioritizing edge cases and risky integrations is not in it: a suite that covers only happy paths with no coverage target meets TST-011 and not this.
FG-M-1c4fc44b5e || cls=XP mod=SHOULD dom=PE rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=pipeline author; act=prefer promoting the same tested artifact through environments; trig=when the deployment model supports artifact promotion; scope=ci-cd skill; exc=model does not support it; time=pipeline; enf=text || test=No oracle counterpart. The condition must be kept.
FG-M-d0b6a09cce || cls=XP mod=SHOULD dom=PE rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=deployment author; act=generated migration scripts are often preferable; trig=controlled production deployment; scope=ef-core skill; exc=often; time=deployment; enf=text || test=Direction is stated, hedged by often. WF-019 asks for an explicit operation, not scripts. A bundle or a controlled CLI step meets it.
FG-M-cf7afce3d7 || cls=MX mod=DEFAULT dom=PE rel=PE pol=GOV-012~ conf=M || actor=test author; act=test the risks that matter; keep test infrastructure proportional; trig=test planning; scope=testing skill; exc=none; time=test design; enf=text || test=Proportional infrastructure follows GOV-012. Test the risks that matter is extra.
FG-M-9c4198ffd3 || cls=XP mod=DEFAULT dom=PE rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=implementer; act=decide whether a cache failure falls back, fails or returns stale; trig=cache in use; scope=caching skill; exc=none; time=design; enf=text || test=RUN-018 limits fallback but does not ask to decide this. Implicit behavior with acceptable semantics meets it.
FG-M-3d675edb0a || cls=XW mod=MUST dom=WF rel=NE pol=- conf=M || actor=agent; act=ensure relevant verification has completed before pushing; trig=before pushing; scope=git-workflow; exc=none; time=before push; enf=text || test=WF-003 says before declaring complete, not before pushing. A push of a work branch before verify meets WF-003 and breaks this.
